# Bluestone Fluency — keep the playbook current

Required skill: **bluestone-fluency** (PIM model, MAPI/PAPI, PBC). Do not invent a generic PIM.

Find it in this order:

1. The installed Cursor/agent skill `bluestone-fluency` (often `~/.cursor/skills/bluestone-fluency`).
2. `BLUESTONE_FLUENCY_PATH` in `.env` if the user set it.
3. A local clone of [bluestone-pim-ai-devkit-public](https://github.com/leafleaf90/bluestone-pim-ai-devkit-public) at `skills/bluestone-fluency/`.

If none of those exist, **stop**. Ask the user to install Fluency:

```bash
npx skills add leafleaf90/bluestone-pim-ai-devkit-public@bluestone-fluency
```

or clone https://github.com/leafleaf90/bluestone-pim-ai-devkit-public and point Cursor at `skills/bluestone-fluency/`. Do not guess a machine path.

When this session learns a PIM fact (FAMILY/GROUP/VARIANT, CLA, VLA, inherit, mandatory, relation vs attribute, completeness, MAPI, PBC, where a value belongs):

1. Read `SKILL.md` in that folder and the relevant linked file (`model.md`, `gotchas.md`, …).
2. If it is a durable **generic** rule and the folder is a writable DevKit clone, add it to `model.md` / `gotchas.md` / `recipes.md` / `auth.md`.
3. If it is tied to a named project, append a dated row to gitignored `insights.internal.md` only when that file’s repo exists. Never put customer names in the public playbook.
4. Do this before ending the turn. Do not wait to be asked.
